<!--
    The Chonkestrel mod's English text, appended to vanilla's
    text_blueprints.xml: the text its data refers to by key (<text id="..."/> and
    so on). The translations are in text-<lang>.xml.append (see
    doc/tools/translations.md).
-->

<!-- BEGIN text of blueprints.xml.append (see tools/extract_mod_text.py) -->
<text name="xftl_ship_PLAYER_SHIP_CHONKESTREL_class">Chonkestrel</text>
<text name="xftl_ship_PLAYER_SHIP_CHONKESTREL_name">The Chonkestrel</text>
<text name="xftl_ship_PLAYER_SHIP_CHONKESTREL_desc">A much bigger take on the Kestrel, with room for eighteen crew, eight weapons and two of nearly every system. It's twice the size of the ships it meets, so they come in pairs.</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_HIVE_CORE_title">Devourer Hive-Core</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_HIVE_CORE_desc">The Lanius hive-ship's still-living core. One asteroid in four that hits the ship is eaten, repairing a point of hull instead of doing damage.</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_COMMAND_CODES_title">Vigilance Command Codes</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_COMMAND_CODES_desc">The blockade's command codes. Rebel automated ships in the second act hesitate when they see them: their weapons charge 20% slower.</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_RELAY_SHARD_title">Chorus Relay Shard</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_RELAY_SHARD_desc">A shard of the Stormbreaker's relay dish, still humming. The crew hear the Chorus coming: they can't be mind controlled for the first 10 seconds of a fight.</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_OSSUARY_SCHEMATICS_title">Ossuary Schematics</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_OSSUARY_SCHEMATICS_desc">The salvage ark's reclamation schematics. A destroyed enemy ship's drones are salvaged as drone parts: one for each drone it had.</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_RADIATION_SHIELDING_title">Radiation Shielding</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_RADIATION_SHIELDING_desc">Lead-lined bulkheads from a research station at the heart of the Radiation Fields. Radiation nebulas don't hurt anyone aboard the ship.</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_PHANTOM_PROJECTOR_title">Phantom Projector</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_PHANTOM_PROJECTOR_desc">A derelict's sensor-ghost projector, from the Mirage Expanse. For the first 12 seconds of each fight, phantom copies of the ship draw the enemies' fire: they miss far more often.</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_DEEP_FIELD_SENSORS_title">Deep-Field Sensors</text>
<text name="aug_XFTL_DEEP_FIELD_SENSORS_desc">Sensors from a dreadnought lost in the Dark Reach, built to see through nebulas too thick for light. The sensors work in a nebula.</text>
<!-- END text of blueprints.xml.append -->

